## Booting the library

Replace `YOUR_USER/YOUR_REPO` with your own GitHub details after you upload `source.lua`.

```lua
local Lumen = loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YOUR_USER/YOUR_REPO/refs/heads/main/source.lua", true))()
```

## Creating a window

```lua
local Window = Lumen:CreateWindow({
	Name = "My Hub",
	Subtitle = "v1.0",
	ToggleKey = Enum.KeyCode.RightShift, -- show / hide the window
	ConfigFolder = "MyHub",              -- folder used for configs and keys
	Size = UDim2.fromOffset(640, 420),   -- optional

	KeySystem = false,
	KeySettings = {},                    -- see "Key system"
})
```

| Setting | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `Name` | string | `"Lumen Window"` | Title shown in the top bar. |
| `Subtitle` | string | `""` | Small text on the right of the top bar. |
| `Size` | UDim2 | `640 x 420` | Window size. It shrinks to fit small screens. |
| `ToggleKey` | KeyCode | `RightShift` | Key that shows or hides the window. |
| `ConfigFolder` | string | `"Lumen"` | Folder for saved configs and keys. |
| `KeySystem` | boolean | `false` | Require a key before the window opens. |
| `KeySettings` | table | `{}` | Key system options. |

Window methods:

```lua
Window:SetVisible(true)
Window:Toggle()
Window:SetToggleKey(Enum.KeyCode.K)
Window:Destroy()
```

## Tabs and sections

```lua
local Main = Window:CreateTab({ Name = "Main", Icon = "★" }) -- Icon is optional, any short text or emoji

Main:CreateSection("Combat") -- returns a Section
```

`CreateSection` returns a section object. It has all the same `Create...` methods as a tab, so these two lines are equivalent:

```lua
Main:CreateButton({ Name = "Hello" })

local Section = Main:CreateSection("Extras")
Section:CreateButton({ Name = "Hello" })
```

Sections add a heading. Elements keep appearing in the order you create them.

`Tab:Activate()` switches to a tab. The first tab you create opens automatically.

## Elements

Every element is created on a tab or a section. Every element returns an object with `:Set(...)` and `:Destroy()`.

Elements that store a value (Toggle, Slider, Input, Bind, Dropdown, ColorPicker) take an optional **flag** as the second argument. Flagged elements are saved by configs and available in `Lumen.Options`.

### Button

```lua
local Button = Main:CreateButton({
Name = "Teleport",
Description = "Optional description",
Callback = function()
print("Clicked")
end,
})

Button:Set({ Name = "New name" })
```

### Toggle

```lua
local Toggle = Main:CreateToggle({
Name = "God Mode",
Description = "Optional",
CurrentValue = false,
Callback = function(value) -- boolean
print(value)
end,
}, "GodMode")

Toggle:Set(true)
print(Toggle.CurrentValue)
```

### Slider

```lua
local Slider = Main:CreateSlider({
Name = "WalkSpeed",
Range = { 16, 200 },
Increment = 1,
Suffix = " studs",
CurrentValue = 16,
Callback = function(value)
print(value)
end,
}, "WalkSpeed")

Slider:Set(100)
```

### Input

```lua
local Input = Main:CreateInput({
Name = "Target",
PlaceholderText = "Username",
CurrentValue = "",
Numeric = false,         -- digits only
MaxCharacters = 20,      -- optional
Enter = false,           -- true: callback only fires when Enter is pressed
ClearOnFocusLost = false,
Callback = function(text)
print(text)
end,
}, "Target")

Input:Set("Roblox")
```

### Bind (keybind)

```lua
local Bind = Main:CreateBind({
Name = "Fly",
CurrentBind = "F",       -- name of an Enum.KeyCode
HoldToInteract = false,  -- false: toggles true/false each press. true: true while held
Callback = function(active)
print(active)
end,
OnChangedCallback = function(keyCode)
print("Rebound to", keyCode.Name)
end,
}, "FlyBind")
```

Click the key box to rebind. Press `Escape` to cancel.

### Dropdown

```lua
local Dropdown = Main:CreateDropdown({
Name = "Mode",
Options = { "Legit", "Rage", "Silent" },
CurrentOption = "Legit",     -- string, or a table when MultipleOptions = true
MultipleOptions = false,
SpecialType = nil,           -- "Player" fills the list with players and keeps it updated
Callback = function(value)   -- string, or a table of strings when MultipleOptions = true
print(value)
end,
}, "Mode")

Dropdown:Set("Rage")
Dropdown:Refresh({ "A", "B", "C" })          -- replace the options
Dropdown:Refresh({ "A", "B" }, true)         -- keep the current selection
```

The dropdown has a built-in search box.

### Color Picker

```lua
local Picker = Main:CreateColorPicker({
Name = "ESP Colour",
Color = Color3.fromRGB(98, 120, 255),
Callback = function(color) -- Color3
print(color)
end,
}, "ESPColour")

Picker:Set(Color3.fromRGB(255, 0, 0))
```

The picker has an HSV square, a hue bar and a hex box.

### Label

```lua
local Label = Main:CreateLabel({ Text = "Hello", Style = "Default" }) -- Default, Info, Success, Warning, Error
Label:Set("New text")
```

### Paragraph

```lua
local Paragraph = Main:CreateParagraph({ Title = "About", Text = "Long text wraps and grows automatically." })
Paragraph:Set({ Title = "New title", Text = "New text" })
```

